s Home Tenure Track Faculty Position in the School of Nursing Home Tenure Track Faculty Position in the School of Nursing Return To Homepage Tenure Track Faculty Position in the School of Nursing Koç University School of Nursing, located in the Health Sciences Campus at Topkapı, aims to achieve excellence in education, research, and practice by bringing together the best students, faculty, and researchers with a value-added approach, and invites academics in Women’s Health Nursing (2 faculty members), Public Health Nursing (1 faculty member) and Nursing Management (2 faculty members) to apply for full-time faculty positions. REQUIREMENTS: Applicants must; have a Bachelor, Master and PhD Degree in Nursing, have a strong teaching background as well as a demonstrated research experience or potential, be competent in giving lectures in Turkish and English, submit at least 85 scores in English YÖKDİL/YDS or an equivalent international language exam accepted by the Higher Education Council (YÖK). RESPONSIBILITIES: Giving lectures in undergraduate and graduate programs, Advising undergraduate and graduate students, Building research capacity, Carrying out certified training programs at SANERC (Semahat Arsel Nursing Education, Practice and Research Center). Candidates are kindly requested to send the following documents via e-mail to hemsirelik@ku.edu.tr . A letter of intent An up-to-date CV Lists of publications Contact information for three references Koç University School of Nursing Health Sciences Campus, Davutpaşa Cd. No:4, 34010 Zeytinburnu/Istanbul/Turkey Rumelifeneri Yolu 34450 Sarıyer, İstanbul / TR information@ku.edu.tr Tel: +90 212 338 1000 MENU Research Academics Explore Contact Admission QUICK MENU Prospective Student KU Student Faculty Member KU Alumni Administrative Staff Visitor Information on Personal Data Privacy Download KUHub Mobile! English Cookie Policy Cookies are used to personalize content and ads, to provide social media features and to analyze our