nstructor Position in English Language Center Home Instructor Position in English Language Center Return To Homepage Instructor Position in English Language Center ESL/EFL Instructor Koç University is one of the premier research institutions in Turkey. Its English Language Center (ELC) provides intensive language instruction to prepare students for the university’s English-medium academic programs. It plays a pivotal role in the students’ transition to university life with approximately 900 students enrolled each year and 50 faculty members. The ELC invites applications from motivated and experienced English language instructors who would like to join a professional academic program. Required Qualifications An MA degree in English Language Teaching/TESOL or a relevant subject. At least two years of teaching experience in higher education. Previous experience as an ESL/EFL teacher. Knowledge of various methods of teaching English to non-native speakers. Great organizational and communication skills. Collaboration with colleagues to provide a positive learning experience to students. Applicants experienced in curriculum, assessment and educational technology are particularly encouraged to apply. Contractual Benefits The ELC offers one-year contracts, renewable, on an annual basis. Benefits may include private health insurance, transportation allowance while residing abroad, and an annual home-visit flight ticket allowance to the instructor’s home country for non-local instructors. Application Requirements: An up-to-date curriculum vitae and the names and contact information for at least three references. A cover letter detailing your qualifications and skills relevant to the position. Statement of teaching philosophy (2 pages maximum). Application documents should be sent to elc@ku.edu.tr Rumelifeneri Yolu 34450 Sarıyer, İstanbul / TR information@ku.edu.tr Tel: +90 212 338 1000 MENU Research Academics Explore Contact Admission QUICK MENU Prospective Student KU Student