Tenure Track Faculty Position in the Law School Home Tenure Track Faculty Position in the Law School Return To Homepage Tenure Track Faculty Position in the Law School Koç University invites applications for full-time faculty positions in the Law School. Koç University is a private, non-profit institution of higher education, founded in 1993. It has been ranked as the best university in Türkiye, 52 nd in Young University Rankings and has been placed among the top 400 universities in the World University Rankings, by the Times Higher Education in 2024. Koç University is on a state-of-the-art campus at Rumelifeneri, Sarıyer, overlooking the Black Sea, close to the city of Istanbul. The University is committed to the pursuit of excellence in both research and teaching. Its aim is to provide world class education and research opportunities to a high-quality group of students by distinguished faculty. More detailed information about Koç University can be found on the University’s web site: http://www.ku.edu.tr Koç University has a fast-growing and dynamic law school which was founded in 2003 and has recruited excellent talents at all levels in recent years ( https://law.ku.edu.tr/en/people/faculty ). As of 2025, the number of students admitted per year is 127, 24 of which have full scholarship. Students with full scholarship were recruited from the top 500 students in Turkey. The Law School has two research centers, namely Dr. Nusret-Semahat Arsel Center for International Business Law (NASAMER: http://nasamer.ku.edu.tr) and Center for Global Public Law (KUREMER: http://kuremer.ku.edu.tr) The Law School members are also engaged in interdisciplinary centers and forums established at Koç University. The Law School’s curriculum follows the national regulatory framework for legal education. The medium of instruction is both English and Turkish. The courses with international and comparative law content, and liberal arts courses are taught in English, whereas courses on Turkish law are taught in Turkish. The Law School offers both LLM and PhD programs in law. Detailed information on Koç University Law School can be found on the web site: http://law.ku.edu.tr Qualifications required from the applicants include a strong commitment to scholarly research with international impact, and high-quality teaching . Candidates should hold a Ph.D. degree in law (or be near completion) from an accredited university. Rank is open and salary is competitive. Assistant professors will be offered four-year contracts, whereas associate professors and full professors will be offered five-year contracts, all of which are subject to renewal. A substantial research record is required for senior appointments. The call is open to qualified candidates specializing in any field of law ; however, preference will be given to applicants specializing in Criminal Law , Civil Law , and Information Technology Law . The deadline for applications is 1 December 2025 . Interested candidates should send a cover letter, current CV, three letters of recommendation, and copies of selected recent publications to vacancyinlaw@ku.edu.tr by e-mail or regular mail. Short-listed candidates will be informed personally in due course for further evaluation. All information on candidates will be kept confidential. Professor Dr. Zeynep Derya Tarman Dean, Law School Koç University Rumelifeneri Yolu, 34450 Sarıyer, İstanbul, Türkiye Phone: 90-212-338 1716-1413 E-mail: vacancyinlaw@ku.edu.tr Rumelifeneri Yolu 34450 Sarıyer, İstanbul / TR information@ku.edu.tr Tel: +90 212 338 1000 MENU Research Academics Explore Contact Admission QUICK MENU Prospective Student KU Student Faculty Member KU Alumni Administrative Staff Visitor Information on Personal Data Privacy Download KUHub Mobile! English Cookie Policy Cookies are used to personalize content and ads, to provide social media features and to analyze our traffic. You can accept all cookies by selecting \"Allow All\" or you can edit the settings