s Pages Home Full-Time Faculty Members of any rank in Clinical Psychology Home Full-Time Faculty Members of any rank in Clinical Psychology Return To Homepage Full-Time Faculty Members of any rank in Clinical Psychology Koç University Department of Psychology has vacancies for full-time faculty positions specializing in Clinical Psychology to commence in Fall 2026. We will consider promising early-career applicants as well as mid-career or senior applicants with an established research agenda. Clinical psychology faculty candidates are expected to have research programs and to teach undergraduate and graduate level courses in clinical psychology in English, supervise clinical practicum in Turkish, and advise MA theses and PhD dissertations. The Department of Psychology at Koç University offers a broad curriculum as indicated on the website (https://cssh.ku.edu.tr/en/programs/psychology/curriculum/). All faculty members, including instructors, are expected to participate fully in departmental responsibilities, including student advising. Located in Istanbul, Turkey, Koç University is a highly reputable English instruction university. Students typically rank in the top percentiles of Turkish high school graduates. The Department of Psychology is the home for strong MA and Ph.D. programs and collaborations with Ph.D. programs of other departments (e.g., neuroscience, design, technology and society, management, and psychiatry). The members of the faculty lead research labs (e.g., mental health lab, trauma and stress studies lab, developmental labs, family labs, cognitive labs, impact evaluation lab), collaborate with faculty members across different disciplines (e.g., medicine, media, design, engineering, sociology), and are members of several research centers (e.g., women and gender studies research center, migration research center, AI center). The application deadline is December 07, 2025. Applicants must submit the application documents : https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/31118 Questions to : İpek Yarar – iyarar@ku.edu.tr Once received, we will acknowledge the receipt of your application. Any questions regarding your application can be directed at the email above and will be answered by a member of the recruitment committee. The application packet should include: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Up to two publications or manuscripts that represent current research Summary statements of research and teaching Names and contact information of three (or more) references (Letters will be requested for short-listed candidates) Application Summary Form Rumelifeneri Yolu 34450 Sarıyer, İstanbul / TR information@ku.edu.tr Tel: +90 212 338 1000 MENU Research Academics Explore Contact Admission QUICK MENU Prospective Student KU Student Faculty Member KU Alumni Administrative Staff Visitor Information on Personal Data Privacy Download KUHub Mobile! English Cookie Policy Cookies are used to personalize content and ads, to provide social media features and to analyze our traffic. You can accept all cookies by selecting \"Allow All\" or you can edit the settings by selecting \"Customize my cookie settings\". When you visit a website, information is stored in your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information may be about you, your preferences or your device, and is often used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually identify you directly, it is meant to provide you with a more personalized web experience. You can choose not to allow some cookies. Click on the different category headings to learn more and change our default settings. Click here to view our cookie policy. Allow All Reject All Customize My Cookie Settings Necessary Cookies These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be turned off in our systems. Statistical Cookies These cookies are used to provide insight into how we can improve our service to all our users and to understand how you interact with our websi