n To Homepage Previous Pages Home Tenure-Track  Faculty Positions in the Department of Chemistry and KUHyTech Center Home Tenure-Track  Faculty Positions in the Department of Chemistry and KUHyTech Center Return To Homepage Tenure-Track  Faculty Positions in the Department of Chemistry and KUHyTech Center The Department of Chemistry, in collaboration with Koç University Hydrogen Technologies Center ( KUHyTech ), in Istanbul, Türkiye, invites applications for a full-time faculty position. We seek a highly motivated candidate with expertise and a documented track record of outstanding research in the chemistry of green energy with potential to be applied to hydrogen technologies, encompassing production, storage, and utilization; especially in the area of membrane technologies for energy applications. The ideal candidate will complement and expand the Department of Chemistry and KUHyTech’s current research activities, which include polymeric and nanostructured materials, organic chemistry, solid-state chemistry, surface science, catalysis, electro-photo-thermo-chemical energy conversion, and theoretical chemistry. Post-doctoral experience is required for candidates at the Assistant Professor level. The successful candidate’s research is expected to align closely with KUHyTech’s mission, driving innovation in hydrogen and energy-related technologies. Koç University is dedicated to excellence in both research and teaching and is ranked 1st in Türkiye, 52th globally in the Times Higher Education Young University Rankings (2024), and 41st Interdisciplinary Science Rankings. Koç University fosters an outstanding interdisciplinary research environment for the faculty members and houses state-of-the art central facilities and multidisciplinary research centers. Koç University as a leading Research University in Türkiye and a center of excellence is hosting 28 out of 48 European Research Council (ERC) Grant recipients in Türkiye and received the largest total amount of research funding from Horizon 2020 in the nation. Faculty members in Turkish Universities are eligible to apply for European Union Marie-Curie Actions and Turkish Science Foundation TUBITAK 2232 International Fellowship for Outstanding Researchers Program. Candidates are expected to develop a competitive research program and to teach both undergraduate and graduate-level courses. The medium of teaching is English. Salary will be competitive and commensurate with experience. University housing or rental subsidy, and K-12 education subsidy will be provided. Applications should be submitted online at academicjobsonline.org and should consist of the following materials: (a) cover letter (including a summary of past and ongoing research) (b) curriculum vitae and publication list, (c) research plan, (d) teaching statement, and (e) three letters of recommendation. Applications submitted by March 09, 2025, will receive full consideration. Applications received later will be reviewed as needed until the positions are filled. Rumelifeneri Yolu 34450 Sarıyer, İstanbul / TR information@ku.edu.tr Tel: +90 212 338 1000 MENU Research Academics Explore Contact Admission QUICK MENU Prospective Student KU Student Faculty Member KU Alumni Administrative Staff Visitor Information on Personal Data Privacy Download KUHub Mobile! English Cookie Policy Cookies are used to personalize content and ads, to provide social media features and to analyze our traffic. You can accept all cookies by selecting \"Allow All\" or you can edit the settings by selecting \"Customize my cookie settings\". When you visit a website, information is stored in your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information may be about you, your preferences or your device, and is often used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually identify you directly, it is meant to provide you with a more personalized web experience. You can choose not to allow some cookies. Click on the different category headings to learn more and change our default settings. Click here to view our cookie policy. Allow All Reject All Customize My Cookie Settings Necessary Cookies These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be turned off in our systems. Statistical Cookies These cookies are used to provide insight into how we can improve our service to all our users and to understand how you interact with our website as an anonymous user. Targeting Cookies These cookies are used to create your profile and provide ads relevant to your interests. It is also used to limit the number of times you see an ad, as well as help measure the effectiveness of the ad campaign. Save My Preferences and Continue Accessibility Tool Navigation Adjustment Hide Images Screen and  Text Reader Motion Reduction Content Adjustment Cursor Enlarge the cursor and change its color White Black Font Sizing Increase and decrease the font size. Font Size Line Spacing Letter Spacing Text Magnifier Reading Guide Image Description Color Adjustment Custom Color Change the site's color. Background Headings Content Adjustment Reset Colors Contrast High Saturation Low Saturation Reset View"
